---
title: Owned process trees and physical lease handoff (implemented)
---
stateDiagram-v2
  direction LR
  state "Owned process (ProcessPhase)" as Process {
    state "Launching" as PLaunching
    state "Running" as PRunning
    state "Stopping" as PStopping
    state "Reaped" as PReaped
    state "Uncertain" as PUncertain
    state "Failed" as PFailed
    state "Lost" as PLost
    [*] --> PLaunching : preflight, authorize_dispatch and launch intent in one unit of work
    PLaunching --> PRunning : native identity recorded (pid, birth token, group or job)
    PLaunching --> PFailed : spawn failed, nothing ran
    PRunning --> PStopping : cancel or shutdown
    PStopping --> PReaped : empty within grace, or killed and verified within the bound
    PStopping --> PUncertain : not verifiable within the bound
    PRunning --> PReaped : boot recovery, vanished or alive and killed
    PRunning --> PUncertain : boot recovery could not establish it
    PLaunching --> PLost : boot recovery, no identity was recorded
    PUncertain --> PReaped : confirm_stopped, a person's recorded statement
    PLost --> PReaped : confirm_stopped, a person's recorded statement
  }
  state "Lease (LeasePhase)" as Lease {
    state "Waiting" as LWaiting
    state "Held" as LHeld
    state "Releasing" as LReleasing
    state "Uncertain" as LUncertain
    state "Released" as LReleased
    [*] --> LWaiting : acquire, priority then FIFO
    LWaiting --> LHeld : promoted with the next fencing token
    LWaiting --> LReleased : waiter Cancelled or Expired
    LHeld --> LReleased : released, or a logical lease Expired
    LHeld --> LReleasing : a physical lease released while it may still be in use
    LHeld --> LUncertain : a physical lease past expiry, owner unreachable, or of a prior boot
    LReleasing --> LReleased : Reconciled once every serving tree settled
    LUncertain --> LReleased : Reconciled once the owner is verified quiescent
    LReleased --> [*]
  }
  note right of Lease
    Capacity stays taken until reconciliation.
    Only then is the next waiter granted (handoff).
    Stale fences are refused at dispatch, renew and release.
  end note
